From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: OpenWrt RTL8197F bringup <noreply@example.invalid>
Date: Sat, 30 May 2026 00:00:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] mips: realtek: force RTL8197F to little endian

RTL8197F/RD05 boots a little-endian MIPS24Kc kernel.  The inherited
Realtek RTL83xx platform Kconfig still advertises big-endian support, and
because the MIPS endian choice has no platform default, oldconfig can keep or
select CPU_BIG_ENDIAN.

For this RD05 bring-up tree, make the Realtek machine little-endian only and
also add an explicit default for RTL8197F in the MIPS endian choice.  This
prevents the kernel from silently being rebuilt as big-endian while the
OpenWrt target/toolchain is mipsel.
---
--- a/arch/mips/Kconfig
+++ b/arch/mips/Kconfig
@@ -629,7 +629,6 @@ config MACH_REALTEK_RTL
 	select IRQ_MIPS_CPU
 	select SYS_HAS_CPU_MIPS32_R1
 	select SYS_HAS_CPU_MIPS32_R2
-	select SYS_SUPPORTS_BIG_ENDIAN
 	select SYS_SUPPORTS_LITTLE_ENDIAN
 	select SYS_SUPPORTS_32BIT_KERNEL
 	select SYS_SUPPORTS_MIPS16
@@ -1139,4 +1138,5 @@ choice
 	prompt "Endianness selection"
+	default CPU_LITTLE_ENDIAN if RTL8197F
 	help
 	  Some MIPS machines can be configured for either little or big endian
 	  byte order. These modes require different kernels and a different
